From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duranaaron <aaronduran2107@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 16:38:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Async block reads for LevelChunkSection

Adds a way to read blocks from another thread without copying the
chunk section.

- LevelChunkSection#getBlockStateAsync(x, y, z): reads a block from
  any thread. Each read is valid, but reading a whole section is not
  one snapshot.
- LevelChunkSection#getBlockModificationCount(): goes up when a block
  in the section changes, so you can skip sections that did not
  change.

Also fixes a race on ARM where a reader could see a palette index
before the palette entry itself ("Palette index out of bounds").
Palettes now use a memory fence when they add an entry. That is rare,
so normal block writes are not slower.

